# Patch: Fix deduplication test to assert saveCall.called unconditionally

## Metadata
adw_id: `11`
review_change_request: `Issue #2: Deduplication test uses 'if (saveCall.called) { expect } else { expect.fail }' instead of asserting saveCall.called unconditionally. Functionally correct but reduces test clarity and CI output readability. Resolution: Replace with expect(saveCall.called).to.be.true; then assert savedFragment.title unconditionally. Severity: tech_debt`

## Issue Summary
**Original Spec:** N/A
**Issue:** The `'deduplicates title when it already exists in the folder'` test wraps its core assertions in an `if (saveCall.called)` branch with a matching `else { expect.fail(...) }`. This is functionally equivalent but produces less readable CI output and obscures intent — Mocha/Chai will not identify which assertion failed as clearly.
**Solution:** Replace the conditional block with `expect(saveCall.called).to.be.true;` followed by unconditional extraction of `saveCall.firstCall.args[0]` and assertion on its `title`.

## Files to Modify

- `studio/test/mas-repository.test.js` — lines 1535–1543

## Implementation Steps
IMPORTANT: Execute every step in order, top to bottom.

### Step 1: Replace the conditional assertion block with unconditional assertions
In `studio/test/mas-repository.test.js`, locate the block at lines 1535–1543:

```js
const saveCall = repo.aem.sites.cf.fragments.save;
if (saveCall.called) {
    const savedFragment = saveCall.firstCall.args[0];
    expect(savedFragment.title).to.equal('lucy-card-1');
} else {
    // save was not called means uniqueTitle === result.title; that means
    // deduplication didn't trigger — which would be a bug.
    expect.fail('save should have been called with the deduplicated title');
}
```

Replace it with:

```js
const saveCall = repo.aem.sites.cf.fragments.save;
expect(saveCall.called).to.be.true;
const savedFragment = saveCall.firstCall.args[0];
expect(savedFragment.title).to.equal('lucy-card-1');
```

## Validation
Execute every command to validate the patch is complete with zero regressions.

1. Verify JS syntax: `node --check studio/test/mas-repository.test.js`
2. Run the relevant test suite: `npm run test:unit -- --grep "deduplicates title"` (or equivalent mocha command in the project)
3. Confirm no `if (saveCall.called)` pattern remains in the file: `grep -n "if (saveCall.called)" studio/test/mas-repository.test.js` — should return no output

## Patch Scope
**Lines of code to change:** ~7 lines removed, ~3 lines added (net -4)
**Risk level:** low
**Testing required:** Run the single unit test `'deduplicates title when it already exists in the folder'` and confirm it passes with a clear assertion error message on failure

